## Canonical Document Lifecycle (Happy Path)

1. Document arrival
2. Filing (match to patient + metadata)
3. Coding (extract information + add codes)
4. Handover (forward as task with highlighting/colour conventions)
5. Clinician action
6. Document task complete (actions completed; task trail remains visible)

**Key determinant of positive flow:** accuracy of system suggestions.

**Suggestion priority:**
- Safety-critical: suggested actions, suggested codes
- Efficiency: patient match, duplicate detection, document type, date, source/department, actions, codes

**Accuracy benchmark:** Human-level accuracy, benchmarked against best human performance; gold standard defined by a dual review panel.

**Autosave:** System must autosave state so users can resume after interruptions without data loss.

**Definition of done:** A document is fully done when there is no further work required.

