## Parking Lot

### 🟡 Important — Must Revisit Before Final Outputs
- **PCN requirements:** parked; solution should be PCN-ready in future but GP-first for V1
- **GP admin templating:** explicitly parked
- **SaMD boundary definition:** formal confirmation required pre go-live; constrain AI feature claims accordingly
- **Task trail permanence (REQ-010):** Whether completed task trails remain permanently visible or can be archived is clinically sensitive. Working assumption: permanently visible. Must be confirmed in V1e Clinical Safety review.
- **Patient match — binary model (REQ-011):** Patient matching is binary: Matched or Unmatched. No confidence score. The NHS Number (Modulus 11 validated) is the primary matching signal; where no valid NHS Number is extractable, or no patient record matches, the document is routed to the unmatched queue.
- **Provisional clinician visibility on auto-match (REQ-011):** Proposal to allow provisional document visibility before match confirmation. Blocked pending formal clinical safety analysis and explicit CSO sign-off. Do not implement without sign-off.
- **OCR/AI metadata suggestions for filing (REQ-012):** Administrative metadata derivation using OCR/AI with mandatory human confirmation is in scope for Documents Management Core. Not SaMD when: (a) human confirmation is required for all suggestions, (b) function is limited to administrative metadata and not clinical coding. EMIS regulatory team to confirm this position in writing before Production release. Narrow validation only — see REQ-012 SaMD Position section.

### 🔴 Legal Blocker — Go-To-Market Gate
- **Metadata-based routing rules (REQ-010):** Practice-configurable routing rules raise a potential conflict-of-interest concern: if EMIS ships or recommends default rule configurations, this could be characterised as clinical practice guidance, which EMIS is not authorised to provide. **Written legal opinion required from EMIS Head of Regulatory + General Counsel before this feature can go live.** This is a go-live blocker for the routing rules capability. See REQ-010 for full documentation.

### 🔴 Architectural Blocker — Requires V1b Resolution
- **EMIS Web audit trail compatibility (REQ-009):** EMIS-X currently has no native audit trail; entries are filed into EMIS Web. V1b must confirm whether EMIS Web audit trail supports all required document management fields, whether entries are queryable from EMIS-X, and whether EMIS Web unavailability can cause silent audit entry loss. This is a DCB0129 and UK GDPR compliance requirement.

### ⚪ To Verify (Non-Blocking)
- Docman integration behaviours (versioning visibility, annotation sync)

